\ETitle{Multi-depot collaborative routing model and algorithm under time-varying carbon intensity}
\EAuthor{ZHOU Leixishu, GAN Hongcheng, QIU Yingying}{Business School, University of Shanghai for Science and Technology, Shanghai 200093, China}
\EAbstract{%
Regional and intercity delivery is complicated by independent depot operations, mixed fleets, charging periods misaligned with grid carbon intensity, and dynamic orders.
This study formulates a collaborative multi-depot mixed-fleet routing model with dynamic demand and time-varying charging emissions.
A two-layer structure of feasible delivery trips and physical-vehicle schedules represents multi-trip connections, inter-trip charging, participation constraints, and rolling-state inheritance while accounting for operating and carbon costs.
A Multi-View Hybrid Genetic Search with Time-Limited MIP Route-Pool Recombination (MV-HGS-SP) is developed.
Mechanism-view decomposition, full-model adjudication, and time-limited route-pool recombination improve solution quality.
Public benchmarks and simulations for three Chinese urban agglomerations verify algorithm effectiveness.
Mechanism experiments examine carbon trading, objective settings, delivery modes, charging timing, participation guarantees, and dynamic orders.
